    test(DBGAP-063): migrate remaining scratch-daemon rigs to race-safe helper
    
    Census pass over every test file that spawns a duckbrain HTTP daemon. The
    board row's 14-file remaining list was already rolled out in 54a1fed (11
    files now import src/testing/race-safe-daemon; http-help-e2e-httphelp001,
    scoped-stop and unix-socket-flag were triaged as no-migration). This pass
    audited the whole suite again (spawn-class sweep, not filename grep) and
    found one in-scope gap: unix-socket-flag.test.ts spawned four real daemons
    whose teardown used a bare fs.rmSync — one ENOTEMPTY from the daemon's
    post-SIGTERM git flush reds the test from teardown. Its cleanup now uses
    the shared removeTempDirSafely (bounded retry, best-effort orphan).
    
    unix-socket-flag keeps its deliberate rig mechanics: it passes --port=0 as
    a literal (the kernel assigns the port atomically at bind — no
    findFreePort close-and-retry TOCTOU window) and asserts only on the
    child's own captured stdout (the banner names the exact socket path), so
    the child's stdio is the identity proof and no sentinel probe is needed.
    
    Deliberately left un-migrated (each verified, not assumed):
    - http-help-e2e-httphelp001: runs `http --help`, never binds; the test
      asserts that NO bind occurred — a daemon rig would defeat the assertion.
    - scoped-stop: pure unit tests over a fake process table, nothing spawned.
    - orphan-daemon-reaper: asserts reap-planning mechanics; stand-in scripts
      never bind (listening: [] asserted); ports already in the private window.
    - in-process createServer(app).listen(0) suites (src/http/routes/*, cli
      http-* files): the test owns the bound socket and reads its own
      .address().port — no spawn, no race window.
    - CLI subprocess tests (version-cli001, token-roles, remember-*, s3,
      dependency-declaration, autocommit-ops006, embedding hooks): no daemon.
    
    No production code touched; no assertion changed (4/4 in the touched file,
    full suite 212/1730 at baseline, tsc --noEmit clean).
    
    Trailer note: the brief requested co-authoring totalwindupflightsystems
    (the configured author identity itself); per fleet identity law the
    co-author trailer credits the human instead, matching every recent
    duckbrain commit.
    
